Article 17 An insurance institution operating agricultural insurance business shall meet the following conditions:
(1) have a well-established grass-roots service network;
(2) have a specialized agricultural insurance operation department and be equipped with corresponding professional personnel;
(3) have a sound internal control system for agricultural insurance;
(4) have sound agricultural reinsurance and catastrophic risk arrangements and risk response plans;
(5) have solvency that complies with the provisions of the insurance regulatory authority of the State Council;
(6) other conditions prescribed by the insurance regulatory authority of the State Council.
No unit or individual other than an insurance institution may operate agricultural insurance business.

Article 27 Where an insurance institution operating agricultural insurance business commits any of the following acts, the insurance regulatory authority shall order it to make corrections and impose a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 yuan but not more than RMB 500,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, it may restrict its business scope or order it to stop accepting new business:
(1) preparing or providing false reports, statements, documents, or materials;
(2) refusing or obstructing supervision and inspection according to law;
(3) failing to use the approved or recorded agricultural insurance clauses and premium rates in accordance with regulations.

Article 28 Where an insurance institution operating agricultural insurance business, in violation of these Regulations, commits any of the following acts, the insurance regulatory authority shall order it to make corrections and impose a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 yuan but not more than RMB 300,000 yuan; if the circumstances are serious, it may restrict its business scope or order it to stop accepting new business:
(1) failing to manage agricultural insurance business separately from other insurance businesses and independently calculate profits and losses in accordance with regulations;
(2) using the agricultural insurance business to seek improper benefits for other institutions or individuals;
(3) failing to apply for approval of agricultural insurance clauses and premium rates in accordance with regulations.
Where an insurance institution operating agricultural insurance business fails to submit agricultural insurance clauses and premium rates for record in accordance with regulations, the insurance regulatory authority shall order it to make corrections within a time limit; if it fails to make corrections within the time limit, a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 yuan but not more than RMB 100,000 yuan shall be imposed.
